# The Monitor, in order.
#
# This is a SEPARATE document from the User Manual (docs/manual/), built by the same
# tools/build-docs.sh into altairsim-monitor.pdf and shipped beside the manual in the
# package. It was a manual chapter once (docs/manual/monitor.md); it moved out because the
# monitor and the debugger are how you drive altairsim ITSELF -- as opposed to the emulated
# hardware the manual describes -- and the two together outgrew a pair of chapters buried in
# the middle of the book.
#
# The prose chapter, then the generated command reference. ORDER declares the sequence,
# because build-docs.sh reads the chapter list from here and from nowhere else.
#
# ref/commands.md is GENERATED from the binary (the CommandDef table, via
# tools/gen-reference.cpp) and byte-checked by the docs-reference test -- do not edit it by
# hand; run `cmake --build build --target docs-reference`. It reads the altairsim> prompt
# itself, which is why it lives with this document and not in the User Manual's ref dir.
monitor.md
ref/commands.md
